  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Road Rehabilitation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objectives of the project are to: (i) reduce vehicle operating costs and road maintenance costs; (ii) increase the service volume of each road; (iii) improve traffic safety conditions; and (iv) protect the investments in road infrastructure made thus far. The project, through the Feeder Road Study component will: (i) improve development of a programme for the rural road access and circulation in Swaziland for the purposes of meeting the nation&apos;s agricultural, industrial and social development goals; (ii) establish an on-going routine and periodic maintenance programme for the protection of the rehabilitated feeder roads network; and (iii) identify the institution responsible for the administration, monitoring and development of the feeder network and set its roles and responsibilities.</narrative>
  </description>
